# Toast Rules

@docs/components.md — _Toasts_

## Variants

Use `variant` on `toast()` — never `className: 'destructive …'`, or `showErrorToast` / `showSuccessToast` helpers.

| Variant | When |
|---------|------|
| `default` | Success, confirmation (omit `variant`) |
| `error` | Failures; omit `title` for the “Error” fallback |
| `warning` | Caution, rate limits |
| `info` | Neutral info (e.g. clipboard copy) |

## API

```tsx
import { toast } from '@/molecules/Toaster/toast';

toast({ variant: 'error', description: '...' });
toast({ title: 'Saved', description: '...' }); // default
```

Provide a string `title` and/or `description`. Custom actions use `{ label, altText, onClick }`; the renderer dismisses before calling the action. The returned handle exposes only `dismiss()`.

Toasts expire after 3 seconds unless `durationMs` is supplied (cart Undo: 5 seconds; wallet setup/retry: 60 seconds). Use `persistent: true` only for state the user must resolve; never combine it with `durationMs`.

Styling: [`Toast.variants.ts`](src/components/atoms/Toast/Toast.variants.ts) only. Custom actions use the neutral App style. Do not import the internal store, state hook or Radix toast atoms in feature code.
